{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why","id":569667,"title":"Claw: why?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-26T14:55:36-07:00","id":569667,"title":"Claw: why?","content":"Without considering gifts, why a Garour should use Claw (dif. 6) when he can use Bite (Dif. 5)?<br /> In Vampire I usually do not allow Vampires to bite without grappling, but I guess that a Garou has no need to grapple an opponent to bite it (in Crinos he should have enough Reach).<br /> <br /> So, again, not considering gifts, why Clawing instead of Biting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T14:57:14-07:00","id":569682,"title":"","content":"And off course &quot;because I like it&quot; is an answer....do we have any other answer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T15:35:42-07:00","id":569701,"title":"","content":"Claws do one more die of damage, unless you happen to be a particular variety of Fera that does way more damage with chomping (Rokea, for example). This means that Garou need to get one more success to match the damage difference, which is the equivalent of adding two dice, usually.<br /> <br /> The better question, perhaps, is what's up with all those Mokole Archid attack modes that are inferior to the bite and and claw (which both do the same amount of damage)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-26-2015, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:10:36-07:00","id":569720,"title":"","content":"There are also a lot of claw based gifts as well, like silver claws, spur claws (attack only me), wind claws (ignore armor), and such that makes claws extra useful...toss in that some enemies are just too toxic to bite (fomori, some mokole, some vampires, I had a friend argue ratkin)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T17:05:49-07:00","id":569792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=569720#post569720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also a lot of claw based gifts as well, like silver claws, spur claws (attack only me), wind claws (ignore armor), and such that makes claws extra useful...</div> </div> </div> </div>OP specifically ruled out Gifts as a consideration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> toss in that some enemies are just too toxic to bite (fomori, some mokole, some vampires, I had a friend argue ratkin) </div> </div> </div>Mokole don't really get injuriously toxic; Rokea, however, can potentially come from sharks that are, or get the Poisoned Flesh Gift. With Ratkin, however, it's not an arguable thing; the book flat-out states that drinking their blood causes some hellish damage to the imbiber (one level lethal of damage per point of Rage that the Ratkin has).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T17:15:19-07:00","id":569795,"title":"","content":"While Mokole aren't injuriously toxic, the breed book had a trait that allowed for you to run the risk of being paralyzed for 5 minute intervals and then CB 20 seems to have replaced it with a trait that does cause you to give up a round retching because of how bad they taste. Given the fact that Mokole can get silver claws as a generic gift, i'd call giving up even 1 round to a mokole opponent bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T17:22:35-07:00","id":569797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=569795#post569795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Mokole aren't injuriously toxic, the breed book had a trait that allowed for you to run the risk of being paralyzed for 5 minute intervals and then CB 20 seems to have replaced it with a trait that does cause you to give up a round retching because of how bad they taste. Given the fact that Mokole can get silver claws as a generic gift, i'd call giving up even 1 round to a mokole opponent bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas taking a bite from a Rokea can result in the wereshark not having to take any further actions to kill you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T17:31:54-07:00","id":569806,"title":"","content":"Ok...doesn't mean its a great idea to bite a mokole with that archid trait...I'm talking in generals not &quot;which is the worst to bite&quot;, i didn't say biting a Rokea was not a big deal. I was just trying to come up with examples...not sure why the aggro here.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T17:44:53-07:00","id":569810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=569806#post569806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok...doesn't mean its a great idea to bite a mokole with that archid trait...I'm talking in generals not &quot;which is the worst to bite&quot;, i didn't say biting a Rokea was not a big deal. I was just trying to come up with examples...not sure why the aggro here.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Not intended to be aggro. It just seemed an odd juxtaposition to make, like something that would trigger a non-diegetic record scratch sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T17:48:17-07:00","id":569811,"title":"","content":"Alright, that's the problem with print, I can never really get tone off of here. I know mokole (we're both fans we've had talks on here over the year or so) but I'll admit I never could get behind the rokea so really I was just listing things off from top of my head without grabbing books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T19:07:16-07:00","id":569844,"title":"","content":"I think the danger of eating some of your opponents is high on the list. The flesh might be toxic or poisonous. It could be addictive or have other strange properties. Some opponents might be too manlike and therefore violating the Litany.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T03:13:54-07:00","id":570107,"title":"","content":"Plus, while a Crinos form Garou might have a pretty good reach with their teeth, they STILL have a much greater reach with their claws.<br /> <br /> That and, again, claws do more damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T04:19:30-07:00","id":570136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=569844#post569844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the danger of eating some of your opponents is high on the list. The flesh might be toxic or poisonous. It could be addictive or have other strange properties. Some opponents might be too manlike and therefore violating the Litany.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something interesting...although I think it's Storyteller's judgement case by case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=570107#post570107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That and, again, claws do more damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You all keep on saying that....but if one does not consider gifts W20 rules give the same damage to bother Bite &amp; Claw!!!<br /> <br /> They both deal Str +1 !!<br /> <br /> Do I miss anything?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=570107#post570107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, while a Crinos form Garou might have a pretty good reach with their teeth, they STILL have a much greater reach with their claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting....but unfortunately there are no proper Reach rules I am aware of...and the optional &quot;weapon Length&quot; rules are bit &quot;unclear&quot; when one compare bite or Claw vs a sword or an enemy's claw....<br /> In a few words: there 's no proper &quot;Reach&quot; number value to compare stuff (and maybe it's good that way...) but this also means that the Reach argument cannot be taken into account.<br /> <br /> The need for Grappling could maybe lower the Bite damage....but it does not seem to apply to Garou!<br /> In V20 vampires need to Grapple for biting.<br /> In W20 the grapple requirement is not there...but I guess that's because Crinos or Lupus Garou have enough Reach to bite without grapple.<br /> So, without Grapple requirement and without any claw-enhancing gift, what's the advantage of using Claw instead of Bite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T04:37:17-07:00","id":570152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucaCherstich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=570136#post570136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They both deal Str +1 !!<br /> <br /> Do I miss anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you do. Claw's base damage is Str +2 (W20, p. 296, also on the char sheet). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T07:13:38-07:00","id":570243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taci</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=570152#post570152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you do. Claw's base damage is Str +2 (W20, p. 296, also on the char sheet). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I do not have W20 in my hands as I'm out of home...but maybe I have &quot;revised&quot; memories.<br /> Nevertheless, this is senseless: why a wereWOLF claw should do more damage than the bite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T10:15:45-07:00","id":570323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucaCherstich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=570243#post570243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I do not have W20 in my hands as I'm out of home...but maybe I have &quot;revised&quot; memories.<br /> Nevertheless, this is senseless: why a wereWOLF claw should do more damage than the bite?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because GAIA WILLS IT! (shreds through a wall with talons)<br /> <br /> In a metatextual sense, it's for the same reason that Garou Crinos is beefier than Khan Crinos - the Garou were written to be lightning-fast engines of destruction, a chunk of violence right up in your face that could rip you several new ones. Hence, they get huge in their &quot;half-wolf&quot; form instead of being somewhere between wolf and human in size, and the nails get lengthened into killer meathooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T13:07:19-07:00","id":570475,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that Hispo bites for +1 damage over other bites.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Crinos has better claws than fangs due to the design. Hispo is designed better for more forceful bites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T13:13:41-07:00","id":570484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=570475#post570475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that Hispo bites for +1 damage over other bites.<br /> <br /> I'd say that Crinos has better claws than fangs due to the design. Hispo is designed better for more forceful bites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though Hispo also has one less dot of Strength, so it still isn't quite the tradeoff that it might otherwise be; your net result is being half a die worth of damage behind Crinos claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-27-2015, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T13:42:04-07:00","id":570537,"title":"","content":"I was just addressing that the base damage tags are even in Hispo, making it Crinos having better claws probably a factor in that.<br /> <br /> As for the trade-off, it's fairly build-dependent. Hispo has more Dex, so the lower diff and best bite damage might, on average be worth more than the +1 automatic base damage dice in Crinos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T14:14:29-07:00","id":570574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=570537#post570537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just addressing that the base damage tags are even in Hispo, making it Crinos having better claws probably a factor in that.<br /> <br /> As for the trade-off, it's fairly build-dependent. Hispo has more Dex, so the lower diff and best bite damage might, on average be worth more than the +1 automatic base damage dice in Crinos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only with maneuvers. The basic numerical details are build-independent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T16:10:41-07:00","id":570663,"title":"","content":"Biting into Wyrm minions tends to have bad side effects like toxins, wyrm taint, acid to face and sensory organs, sudden growing of a giant maw where your head is ripping flesh away and so on and so forth. Also yes Claws give you more reach than Bites which in itself is a thing and if your fighting something with a knife or a sword (or parrying with claws) do you really want to be leading that attack with your face if you can avoid it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T16:25:40-07:00","id":570675,"title":"","content":"The problem is you have a difficulty on the attack roll difference. The impact on damage of -1 diff and +1 dex for roll over damage varies with base dice pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T03:50:17-07:00","id":571144,"title":"","content":"One point of difficulty averages to 1 sucess per ten dice. Most Garou will probably be somewhere around 8 dice on their attacks (raising dex and brawl are pretty much no-brawners in this game), so it's indeed around 1 success. However, this one success can either add one damage die or add the base damage (if it's the only success rolled or remaining after dodge) or be utterly useless (if the enemy evades the attack). So I'd say: Against an enemy with stats close to yours who can spare actions for defending, the bite is better because of the chance the one additional success is the one that lets your entire attack go through. Against mooks, the claw is better because it's a guaranteed damage die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T05:18:52-07:00","id":571202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=570323#post570323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In a metatextual sense, it's for the same reason that Garou Crinos is beefier than Khan Crinos - the Garou were written to be lightning-fast engines of destruction, a chunk of violence right up in your face that could rip you several new ones. Hence, they get huge in their &amp;quot;half-wolf&amp;quot; form instead of being somewhere between wolf and human in size, and the nails get lengthened into killer meathooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are right. <br /> And Garou Crinos are also stronger than Khan Crinos, so the whole Wolf &amp;Tiger argument is not valid.<br /> Nevertheless, maybe I have odd memories from the 1990s...but wasn't there a time whem Garou Claw dealt Str+1 while Bastet Claw dealt Str+2 ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T06:55:36-07:00","id":571251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucaCherstich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=571202#post571202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you are right.<br /> And Garou Crinos are also stronger than Khan Crinos, so the whole Wolf &amp;Tiger argument is not valid.<br /> Nevertheless, maybe I have odd memories from the 1990s...but wasn't there a time whem Garou Claw dealt Str+1 while Bastet Claw dealt Str+2 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, seeing as how Bastet in the first edition player's guide didn't have any notes about this for their natural attacks. Just that Khan and Simba did Strength + 3 damage with their bite (adjusted to +2 for modern systems with extra attack successes adding to damage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T14:47:56-07:00","id":571910,"title":"","content":"Sometimes you just don't want to get a moutful of Wyrm-juice in your mouth.<br /> Also, reach is longer on a claw attack.<br /> Plus if you grapple with a bite maneuver and hold on, you can still claw with your claws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T00:12:20-07:00","id":572368,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it again, giving &quot;Str+2dmg&quot; to Claw, raises a couple of doubts:<br /> <br /> 1) Klaives.<br /> If they do the same damage of normal crinos claws (Str +2) they are ... not so great.<br /> The silver in them will make you lose 1 Gnosis and it will be an effective weapons only vs shifters (and not all of them).<br /> Certainly Black Spiral Dances will suffer it....but most Banes, Fomori, Vampires, Mages or mere Mortals will just not care about it.<br /> And you lose 1 gnosis anyway...<br /> Without using any klaive-specific maneuver klaives are just not worth their price (and Klaivaskar still does not appear in any w20 book, one should resurrect an old book. Do not remember where it was.).<br /> <br /> <br /> 2) Generic Maneuver.<br /> The &quot;Claw&quot; is not a garour-specific maneuver but it should apply to everybody!<br /> So this means that even normal, mundane Wolves, Alligators or Rats will have Claws (Str +2) dealing more damage than bites (Str +1)!<br /> And this is just silly!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T01:22:28-07:00","id":572435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucaCherstich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=572368#post572368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it again, giving &quot;Str+2dmg&quot; to Claw, raises a couple of doubts:<br /> <br /> 1) Klaives.<br /> If they do the same damage of normal crinos claws (Str +2) they are ... not so great.<br /> The silver in them will make you lose 1 Gnosis and it will be an effective weapons only vs shifters (and not all of them).<br /> Certainly Black Spiral Dances will suffer it....but most Banes, Fomori, Vampires, Mages or mere Mortals will just not care about it.<br /> And you lose 1 gnosis anyway...<br /> Without using any klaive-specific maneuver klaives are just not worth their price (and Klaivaskar still does not appear in any w20 book, one should resurrect an old book. Do not remember where it was.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Klaives are fetishes, not mundane weapons. Most, if not all will have spirits of war or violence bound into them, which makes the klaive do aggro damage to any and all enemies. The most feared klaives will have an additional spirit bound within which will grant even more power. Klaives are not common, and are not necessary for a Garou to fight in defense of Gaia. They are particularly holy weapons, as much a status symbol as deadly implement of war.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Generic Maneuver.<br /> The &quot;Claw&quot; is not a garour-specific maneuver but it should apply to everybody!<br /> So this means that even normal, mundane Wolves, Alligators or Rats will have Claws (Str +2) dealing more damage than bites (Str +1)!<br /> And this is just silly! </div> </div> </div>Claws aren't a maneuver at all, 'claws' are stats for a natural weapon, in the case of Garou Str +2. I don't think any of the creatures listed have claw attacks in their statistics (although I could be wrong, I don't feel like digging through Ways of the Wolf to be sure). I know that in the stats given for gators in the VtM rulebook had no claw attacks and only a fairly strong bite (and a goddamn Pokemon-esque 'tailslap').","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 06-29-2015, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T01:38:34-07:00","id":572438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=572435#post572435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Klaives are fetishes, not mundane weapons. Most, if not all will have spirits of war or violence bound into them, which makes the klaive do aggro damage to any and all enemies. The most feared klaives will have an additional spirit bound within which will grant even more power. Klaives are not common, and are not necessary for a Garou to fight in defense of Gaia. They are particularly holy weapons, as much a status symbol as deadly implement of war.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but:<br /> - Crinos Claw deal Aggro damage too (and the same amount! Str+2) to all enemies!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<br /> - If one take a Klaive he does so ONLY FOR story reasons (and if Storyteller give importance to that) ... given that it's more a bother than anything else (lose 1 gnosis and older Garou will question why you got such a weapon...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T02:09:20-07:00","id":572449,"title":"","content":"You take Klaives for two things... prestige and murdering other Werewolves. Hopefully Black Spiral Dancers. Garou won't question you for having a Klaive as they are the traditional and most glorious weapon of the Garou, and actually owning them gives you bonus renown.<br /> <br /> As for why you use weapons rather then teeth or claws... are you seriously unaware of all the Wyrmish crap you do not want all over your hands or in your mouth? Besides, some people are just better with a gun or an axe they ever will be with claws and teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T02:14:27-07:00","id":572450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=572449#post572449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for why you use weapons rather then teeth or claws... are you seriously unaware of all the Wyrmish crap you do not want all over your hands or in your mouth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Off course I'm not, but that's no rule about it.<br /> It's all Storyteller's Call (given that we do not have any &quot;Taint&quot; rank like L5R or stuff like that).<br /> <br /> And, seriously, how many times have you seen Storytellers give poisons and taint to all Fomori- and bane- biting Garou?<br /> I know it happens but, again, it's an &quot;ad-hoc&quot; decision by the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> So, given the rules as they are, Klaives are useless, unless Storytellers and Players are good ones and play giving a fluff/social and/or mythological meaning to the Klaive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T05:16:19-07:00","id":572528,"title":"","content":"... how exactly is unsoakable, unhealable aggravated damage to 85% of all shifters &quot;useless&quot; ?<br /> <br /> There is such a thing as a Wyrm taint, but if you're not playing it up, and if it's not a requirement for the Garou to be careful and cleanse and Cleanse themselves, then you're doing something wrong. It's right there in the text and the rituals, if you're ignoring it just because it has no hard rules... You're not very familiar with this White Wolf thing, are you?<br /> <br /> I mean the whole concept of Wyrm taint is not clearly mechanically defined and it's one of the core issues of the whole game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T07:06:45-07:00","id":572612,"title":"","content":"I must admit a enjoyed a lot of White Wolf stuff until the early 2000s, then we stop for the last decade or so.<br /> We are resurrecting this thing now.<br /> Maybe after these 10-15 years I'm still confused and mix stuff from different editions, but a few things are clear to me.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, the point is still that &quot;corruption&quot; is &quot;corruption&quot; only if sensible storytellers and players make it meaningful.<br /> I see nothing wrong in saying that.<br /> <br /> I know that even the Rite of Cleansing is useless if Storytellers and Players do not make it useful and meaningful, punishing those who forget &quot;cleaning&quot;.<br /> <br /> Klaive are &quot;great stuff&quot; only if Storytellers and Players play them as they are so.<br /> <br /> And regarding the utility vs shifters, it really depends on the chronicle theme.<br /> One can have whole chronicles of Vampire-fighting or wyrm-fighting without meeting a single enemy shifter but only banes and fomori (although I admit they are useful vs Black Spiral Dancers...but they are not the only wym minions around!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5960,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","user":"LucaCherstich","date":". 06-29-2015, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T09:39:06-07:00","id":572814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nevertheless, the point is still that &quot;corruption&quot; is &quot;corruption&quot; only if sensible storytellers and players make it meaningful. </div> </div> </div>Trashtalking police officers while carrying a small arsenal of unregistered weapons in the trunk of your car is also only a bad idea if storytellers make it meaningful.<br /> <br /> Regarding corruption or poisonings incurred by biting nasty stuff, I don't religiously enforce it, but there have been enough instances that most of the PCs don't do it unless they have Resist Toxin. Claws are relatively safe until we get to the acid blood stuff.<br /> <br /> As for Klaives, yeah, they're not for your everyday wyrm hunt. These are ceremonial and holy weapons. In my game, the PCs have one that is usually left at the Totem Shrine and only taken out when there's an above-average chance of a Spiral encounter - but in that case, they're really glad they have it since it's simply a one-hit-K.O. (or one-hit-send-into-frenzy-second-hit-death) against anything vulnerable to silver. Not being able to use your seven or more soaking dice against the ten or more damage dice just plain sucks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T11:15:42-07:00","id":572936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=572814#post572814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Klaives, yeah, they're not for your everyday wyrm hunt. These are ceremonial and holy weapons. In my game, the PCs have one that is usually left at the Totem Shrine and only taken out when there's an above-average chance of a Spiral encounter - but in that case, they're really glad they have it since it's simply a one-hit-K.O. (or one-hit-send-into-frenzy-second-hit-death) against anything vulnerable to silver. Not being able to use your seven or more soaking dice against the ten or more damage dice just plain sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here. -1 Gnosis is a small price to pay when the Ahroun is killing one or two Black Spiral Dancers every three seconds. Silver be nasty, yo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T12:58:54-07:00","id":573063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/569667-claw-why?p=571910#post571910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes you just don't want to get a moutful of Wyrm-juice in your mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know... I've seen a dog put some <i>nasty</i> things in his mouth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T14:42:07-07:00","id":573193,"title":"","content":"Lacking Klaivaskar does hurt Klaives utility however they are melee weapons meaning that the opponent will more likely want to Dodge instead of Block their attacks which can prove advantageous in some circumstances. Also you get renown for owning a Klaive and for using it for the good of the Sept etc. One quick fix we have employed (when not porting in the Revised Klaivaskar rules) was to allow Klaivaskar as a Specialisation in Melee with the special rule that a Klaivaskar counted 10s as 2 successes on Damage rolls as well as their Attack rolls. It certainly made Klaives most desirable to those who knew how to weild them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T05:01:46-07:00","id":573739,"title":"","content":"Why would you need Klaivaskar to make Klaives good? What does it offer that you cannot map out within the system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T10:40:03-07:00","id":574100,"title":"","content":"It has a bunch of maneuvers that aren't included in the basic rules. Though there's pretty much no reason any of the Garou-specific fighting Abilities are Garou specific. Kailindo requests rapid shapeshifting, but the other two are all things that human fighters should be able to do. A human fencer doesn't need to learn a specialized fighting style to try to cut your forehead and make you bleed into your own eyes. Klaives help in Garou vs. Garou fighting because they can't heal the cut.<br /> <br /> Whether or not it maps to something already in the system, pretty much every Klaivaskar manuever is something that should be a logical extension of Melee without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T23:36:51-07:00","id":576093,"title":"","content":"2nd Edition Klaivaskar had some different rules though Heavy Arms, like reflexively spending rage for Parry actions etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T23:37:33-07:00","id":576095,"title":"","content":"Also Klaivaskar as it's own skill was pretty cool, as it granted (in 2nd and revised) lore on each different Kalive and a few other roleplaying goodness tidbits<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T03:05:03-07:00","id":578485,"title":"","content":"There's no real mechanical advantage to one over the other. My experience is that biting does - on average - do more damage because of the lower difficulty (you're more likely to hit, AND get more successes to add to your damage roll) but it's not enough of a mechanical advantage that clawing is &quot;useless.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for getting &quot;wyrm grossness in you&quot; - I greatly contest that notion. Sure there's a temptation to see every Fomori as a walking barrel of toxic waste hidden inside a leper... but that's really not how it works. Oh sure they might have toxic or damaging powers... but most won't. And corruption is a <i>spiritual</i> malady, not a physical one. Physical contact, even ingestion - with wyrm-critters is not going to send you to hell. If it were, the Garou would either all be Spirals, or would be so busy performing rites of cleansing that they couldn't get anything else done. if you sink your teeth into a fomori, you're not going ot get a spray of instant wyrm corruption to the face. You get blood, flesh, and bone, and nothing else. Granted it's <i>human</i> flesh and bone, so if you gulp some down, that's a problem...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T12:47:46-07:00","id":579080,"title":"","content":"The Wyrm rubs off on everything. No matter how pure and innocent something might be it will weigh upon them and taint them. That's why you never can really rely on Sense Wyrm and why even the Werewolves will end up tainted over time. This is exactly why their spiritual purity and taking care of themselves is paramount to keeping them sane and operatonal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:40:19-07:00","id":584647,"title":"","content":"My players rarely bite fur gnawl is extremely useful for shredding armor something they encounter enough that they usually attempt that. Claws allow you distance, bite is close in and exposes you to both toxic blood, spiritual corruption, and the ever popular second mouth. Certain tribes and gifts however make biting a better option Red Talons, Bone Gnawers, and Fianna are good examples. Bone Gnawers and Red Talons both have Resist Toxin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T15:41:07-07:00","id":605084,"title":"","content":"Because sometimes your fighting something truly disgusting and you don't want that crap in your mouth...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T05:11:28-08:00","id":831673,"title":"","content":"Momentum. Massive arms and upper body strength will launch a claw with a crazy force to its target. You get an impact that cant measure with the &quot;mere&quot; pressure from a bite, which delivers a more controlled force of damage. Claws can litterly end up on the other side of a torsoe, which teeth really cant.<br /> <br /> So Claws are designed for more brutal damage then Fangs.<br /> <br /> Thats how i see it. Momentum. Impact. Penetration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6944-cellcrawler","name":"Cellcrawler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6944_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T05:13:56-08:00","id":831675,"title":"","content":"Ok........?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:24:50-08:00","id":831805,"title":"","content":"Actually, bites are more powerful than impacts. Claws are just more practical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T09:26:39-08:00","id":831807,"title":"","content":"Yeah. So on top of the necro, that's not really how bites vs. claws works in nature. Pretty much everything that uses claws (or something analogous to them) to do &quot;massive&quot; damage is either really going for maximum accuracy (often against much smaller prey items), or doesn't have body design that allows for anything else.<br /> <br /> When something needs to get torn to shreds with high amounts of momentum, impact, and penetration? Nature goes bite. Lions, tigers, and bears (oh my!) all have impressive &quot;upper&quot; body strength, and can easily kill a human with their claws. They all default to bites for killing blows though. Claws are for catching prey and holding on to it/holding it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T16:30:48-08:00","id":833577,"title":"","content":"I got my mind locked in on Crinos form for some odd reason. Thats where you get all them brutal gut penetrating moves and high powerswings :P. Other then that bites naturally does more damage on the same spot. Especially if something bites, holds and shakes. That tissue damage is often way more severe the puncture wounds from K9:s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6944-cellcrawler","name":"Cellcrawler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6944_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}